.Dd July 9, 2026
.Dt CAPABILITIES 7
.Os GergiOS
.Sh NAME
.Nm capabilities
.Nd GergiOS capability model overview
.Sh DESCRIPTION
GergiOS implements a capability-based security model as a refinement
of the existing kernel privilege system. Capabilities provide
fine-grained control over privileged operations.
.Pp
Capabilities are stored as a 64-bit bitmask with 13 defined bits.
Each bit represents a specific privilege.
.Sh CAPABILITY LIST
.Bl -tag -width CAP_FS_DAC_OVERRIDE -compact
.It Sy CAP_SYS_RAWIO
(bit 0) Direct I/O port access. Required for device drivers that
access hardware I/O ports.
.It Sy CAP_NET_RAW
(bit 1) Raw socket access. Required for AF_PACKET sockets.
.It Sy CAP_NET_BIND
(bit 2) Bind to privileged ports (<1024). Required for daemons
listening on standard service ports.
.It Sy CAP_NET_ADMIN
(bit 3) Network interface configuration. Required for
.Xr ifconfig 8 ,
.Xr route 8 .
.It Sy CAP_SYS_ADMIN
(bit 4) System administration. Required for RS control operations.
.It Sy CAP_SYS_BOOT
(bit 5) System reboot/shutdown. Required for
.Xr reboot 8 ,
.Xr shutdown 8 .
.It Sy CAP_IPC_OWNER
(bit 6) Bypass IPC send masks. Allows sending IPC to any process.
.It Sy CAP_FS_MOUNT
(bit 7) Mount/umount filesystems. Required for
.Xr mount 8 ,
.Xr umount 8 .
.It Sy CAP_FS_CHOWN
(bit 8) Change file ownership. Required for
.Xr chown 8 .
.It Sy CAP_FS_DAC_OVERRIDE
(bit 9) Bypass file permission checks (DAC override).
.It Sy CAP_VM_MAP
(bit 10) Map physical memory. Required for device DMA operations.
.It Sy CAP_IRQ_ALLOC
(bit 11) Allocate IRQ lines. Required for interrupt handling.
.It Sy CAP_PCI_ACCESS
(bit 12) PCI configuration space access.
.El
.Sh CAPABILITY SETS
Predefined sets for common service types:
.Bl -tag -width network
.It Sy base
No capabilities. For unprivileged user processes.
.It Sy system
.Nm CAP_NET_BIND , CAP_IPC_OWNER .
For standard system servers.
.It Sy driver
.Nm CAP_SYS_RAWIO , CAP_IRQ_ALLOC , CAP_VM_MAP .
For device drivers.
.It Sy network
.Nm CAP_NET_RAW , CAP_NET_ADMIN , CAP_NET_BIND .
For network services.
.It Sy admin
.Nm CAP_SYS_ADMIN , CAP_SYS_BOOT , CAP_FS_MOUNT .
For administrative tools.
.It Sy all
All 13 capabilities. For core services (RS, VM, PM).
.El
.Sh INHERITANCE RULES
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.Nm fork() :
Child inherits parent's effective, permitted, and bounding sets.
.It
.Nm exec() :
Effective and permitted sets reset to bounding set.
Bounding set unchanged.
.It
.Nm setuid(0) :
No automatic capability elevation. Requires
.Nm CAP_SYS_ADMIN
to raise capabilities.
.El
.Sh API
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#include <sys/capability.h>

int cap_get_proc(cap_t *caps);
int cap_set_proc(const cap_t *caps);
int cap_get_bound(cap_t *caps);
.Ed
.Pp
.Nm cap_t
is a 64-bit unsigned integer.
.Nm cap_get_proc
returns the current process's effective capabilities.
.Nm cap_set_proc
sets the effective and permitted capabilities
(can only drop privileges unless CAP_SYS_ADMIN is held).
.Nm cap_get_bound
returns the bounding set.
.Sh CONFIGURATION
Capabilities are assigned to services in
.Pa /etc/system.conf
using the
.Ic capabilities
directive:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
service myapp
{
    capabilities NET_BIND IPC_OWNER;
    # or: capabilities ALL;
    # or: capabilities NONE;
}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cap_get_proc 2 ,
.Xr cap_set_proc 2 ,
.Xr system.conf 5 ,
.Xr mac-policy 5 ,
.Xr macctl 8
.Sh HISTORY
The GergiOS capability model first appeared in GergiOS 1.0.
